# PHP coding guidelines

**Scope:** Apply only when working on the TastyIgniter app under `app/` (extensions, seed, themes, Docker/PHP there). Do **not** apply to `cdp/` or other sibling projects in this repo.

Follow [TastyIgniter PHP Coding Guidelines](https://tastyigniter.com/docs/resources/php-coding-guidelines) (Spatie-derived). PSR-1 / PSR-2 / PSR-12. Prefer camelCase for string-like names except Model attributes.

## Types and classes

- Prefer `?Type` over `Type|null`. Add `: void` when a method returns nothing.
- Type properties; do not use `@var` docblocks for them. Do not use `final` by default.
- Enum cases: PascalCase. Facades: fully qualified (`Illuminate\Support\Facades\Config`, not `Config`).
- One trait per `use` line. Prefer string interpolation over `.` / `sprintf`.

## Naming (Laravel conventions)

| Kind | Style | Example |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Controller / route / table | plural | `ArticlesController`, `articles/1` |
| Model / object | singular | `User`, `$activeUser` |
| Collection / variable | plural / camelCase | `$activeUsers`, `$anyOtherVariable` |
| Column / FK / config key | snake_case | `meta_title`, `article_id` |
| Method / test method | camelCase | `getAll`, `testGuestCannotSeeArticle` |
| Function / view / config file | snake / kebab | `abort_if`, `show-filtered.blade.php` |
| Job / Event / Listener | action tense | `CreateUser`, `CustomerApproved`, `SendInvitationMailListener` |

## Style preferences

- Prefer helpers over facades (`session()`, `now()`, `redirect()`, `optional()`).
- Prefer Eloquent over Query Builder / raw SQL; Collections over arrays; eager-load relations (`with`) to avoid N+1.
- Fat models, skinny controllers: keep query logic on models / scopes.
- Config files kebab-case; keys snake_case. Never call `env()` outside config — use `config()`.
- User-facing text via `lang(...)`, not hardcoded strings.
- Validation: FormRequest classes; multi-rule fields as arrays (`['nullable', 'date']`), not `|`.
- Artisan command names: kebab-case; print progress / a final success comment.

## Control flow and docs

- Early returns / happy path last; avoid `else` when early return or ternary is clearer.
- Prefer separate `if`s over long compound conditions when debugging matters.
- Curly braces for multi-line `if`; one-line `if` without braces is OK.
- Skip redundant docblocks on fully type-hinted methods. When needed: FQCN, one-line if possible, most common type first in unions.
- Prefer expressive names over comments; blank lines between logical statements, not inside `{}`.

## Blade

- Four-space indent. No space after directives: `@if($condition)`. Minimize raw PHP in templates.
